Text:
The Reconciliator makes the desk
- open the files of some extensions with one program of the Fearless family
- show the icons of those extensions and of the windows of that program.
The 'identity' of the program calling Reconciliator.reconcile is the file name
of the command of that program, without extension.//Looks like an implementation note or just omit
The 'Fearless family' is the set of the identities containing the text "Fearless" or "fearless".
Two different versions, of fearlessManager or of the portable Fearless, never share an identity.//What this even means? what happen if they do? because I suspect in practice they would, with the identity defined as just the file name.
The 'setup' of an identity is every registry key and file that Reconciliator.reconcile writes for that identity.//I suspect this 'setup' term is near never used.

Define Reconciliator.eradicateAll:
A Reconciliator.eradicateAll deletes the setup of every identity of the Fearless family, with no check.

Implementation notes:
Every Reconciliator.reconcile and every Reconciliator.eradicateAll holds, from start to end, the lock of the file fearlessAssociations.lock.
fearlessAssociations.lock is in the folder where the desk keeps the data of the programs the user runs: %LOCALAPPDATA% on Windows, $XDG_DATA_HOME on Linux, ~/Library/Application Support on macOS.
The code of the Reconciliator is the package fileAssociations of Commons.
